@startuml
title Use Case Diagram(Collection Point Counter Work)
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Resident" as Resident
actor "Staff" as Staff
actor "Courier" as Courier

rectangle "Community Parcel Collection Point System" {

  usecase "Log in" as UC_LOGIN
  usecase "Record an exception parcel" as UC_EXCEPTION

  package "Parcel intake" as PKG_INTAKE {
    usecase "Register a courier batch" as UC_INTAKE
    usecase "Get a storage location suggestion" as UC_RECOMMEND
    usecase "Shelve a parcel" as UC_SHELVE
  }

  package "Collection at the counter" {
    usecase "Verify a pickup code" as UC_VERIFY
    usecase "Confirm a handover" as UC_HANDOVER
  }

  package "Resident self service" {
    usecase "Receive an arrival notice" as UC_NOTICE
    usecase "View my parcels" as UC_MY_PARCELS
    usecase "See the storage location and pickup code" as UC_SEE_CODE
  }
}

Courier --> UC_INTAKE : delivers a batch at the counter

Staff --> UC_LOGIN
Staff --> UC_INTAKE
Staff --> UC_SHELVE
Staff --> UC_VERIFY
Staff --> UC_HANDOVER
Staff --> UC_EXCEPTION

Resident --> UC_LOGIN
Resident --> UC_NOTICE
Resident --> UC_MY_PARCELS

UC_MY_PARCELS ..> UC_SEE_CODE : <<include>>
UC_HANDOVER ..> UC_VERIFY : <<include>>

note right of Courier
  External actor. The courier has no account
  and never logs in. Staff record what the
  courier delivers, which is why the courier
  is drawn outside the system boundary.
end note

note bottom of PKG_INTAKE
  The location suggestion inside this package is
  a suggestion only. Staff keep the final decision
  on the shelf position.
end note
@enduml